  "hypothesised_typology": [
    {
      "text": "Hypothesis: a repeating pass-through / layering chain in which funds are collected at 311052 from a small-amount feeder (308639), consolidated and pushed to 311417, then re-broken into a fixed three-transfer set and forwarded to 314950. The repeated use of identical amounts across days is consistent with deliberate value-preserving layering rather than ordinary commercial payment behaviour.",
      "citations": ["call_00_bfQGTEOuSUplMZXIeF8P0005", "call_01_vTPDTXZnvbbhreLBwM7l3525", "call_00_Qg95dGAW1sfKhP4T4Ff84109", "call_01_8c0IPhgaa1Nwk1SZufbr3281"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The corpus describes the related structural risk of payment chains being fragmented into discrete transfers so that institutions in the chain lack full originator/beneficiary information, which impedes screening and monitoring.",
      "citations": ["ref:explanatory-note-for-revised-r-16:016"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The corpus also notes the typology of a payment sent through a financial institution with which the customer does not maintain the account holding the funds, so the true origin of funds is not indicated in the payment message.",
      "citations": ["ref:explanatory-note-for-revised-r-16:017"]
    }
  ],
